### Core Principles

#### 1. Component Selection Priority
**ALWAYS** use components in this order:
1. **Custom Form Components** (`@forms/`) - When available for form controls
2. **Base UI Components** - For navigation, feedback, layout, and data display
3. **Custom implementations** - Only when neither custom nor Base UI components fit

#### 2. Available Custom Form Components
**ALWAYS** prefer these custom components over base Base UI:
- **`ValidatedInput`** - Text, email, password, number, textarea inputs with validation
- **`ValidatedCustomSelect`** - Select dropdown with validation
- **`CustomSelect`** - Basic select dropdown
- **`CustomSelectMulti`** - Multi-select with logic options
- **`CustomCheckbox`** - Checkbox with validation support
- **`SliderControl`** - Slider with value display
- **`ValidatedForm`** - Form container with validation context

#### 3. Styling Approach
- **Use Tailwind CSS** for styling Base UI components
- **Leverage composition** to customize component behavior
- **Maintain accessibility** - Base UI handles ARIA attributes automatically
- **Follow design system** - use consistent spacing, colors, and typography

### Available Components

#### Custom Form Components (PREFERRED)
- **ValidatedInput**: Text, email, password, number, textarea with validation
- **ValidatedCustomSelect**: Select dropdown with validation
- **CustomSelect**: Basic select dropdown
- **CustomSelectMulti**: Multi-select with logic options (OR/AND)
- **CustomCheckbox**: Checkbox with validation support
- **SliderControl**: Slider with value display
- **ValidatedForm**: Form container with validation context
- **useValidatedForm**: Hook for form validation

#### Base UI Components (Use Directly)
**Documentation**: [https://base-ui.com/react/components/](https://base-ui.com/react/components/)

**Form Controls**: 
- Input, Select, Checkbox, Radio, Switch, Number Field, Slider, Field, Fieldset, Form
- **Note**: Prefer custom `@forms/` components over these

**Navigation**: 
- Menu, Navigation Menu, Menubar, Tabs, Breadcrumb
- **Documentation**: [https://base-ui.com/react/components/navigation-menu.md](https://base-ui.com/react/components/navigation-menu.md)

**Feedback**: 
- Dialog, Alert Dialog, Toast, Tooltip, Popover, Context Menu
- **Documentation**: [https://base-ui.com/react/components/dialog.md](https://base-ui.com/react/components/dialog.md)

**Layout**: 
- Accordion, Collapsible, Separator, Scroll Area, Toolbar
- **Documentation**: [https://base-ui.com/react/components/scroll-area.md](https://base-ui.com/react/components/scroll-area.md)

**Data Display**: 
- Progress, Meter, Avatar, Preview Card
- **Documentation**: [https://base-ui.com/react/components/progress.md](https://base-ui.com/react/components/progress.md)

### Success Criteria
- [ ] Custom form components used for all form controls
- [ ] Base UI components used for navigation, feedback, layout, and data display
- [ ] Official Base UI documentation consulted for component usage
- [ ] Consistent Tailwind CSS styling applied
- [ ] Accessibility features maintained
- [ ] Component composition follows patterns
- [ ] Design system colors and spacing used
- [ ] Form validation integrated properly
- [ ] Keyboard navigation works correctly
- [ ] Screen reader compatibility verified

**CRITICAL**: Always prefer custom form components from `@forms/` over base Base UI components for form controls. Use Base UI directly only for navigation, feedback, layout, and data display components. **ALWAYS** consult the official Base UI documentation for proper component usage.
